{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":139382,"duration_api_ms":212064,"num_turns":8,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c9d0d054-0bef-40dd-9154-6e0f3a4955d3","total_cost_usd":0.6153092499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":1422,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29540,"cache_read_input_tokens":155495,"output_tokens":3028,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29540,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":137,"outputTokens":9694,"cacheReadInputTokens":1322085,"cacheCreationInputTokens":71449,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27012674999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1422,"outputTokens":3028,"cacheReadInputTokens":155495,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29540,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.34518249999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all six amendments against the actual codebase. Four amendments (invariant enforcement gaps and stale doc comment) are valid bugs that should be fixed. The worktree-shipping amendment raises a legitimate process concern. The chloride-aware nitrite hazard amendment is factually incorrect — the feature is already fully implemented in the main repo.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-2792298a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: enforce_invariants clamps all other 0-1 indices (biofilter_maturity_index, maturity_index, nuisance_index, population_index, grazing_pressure_index, etc.) but NOT denitrifier_activity_index. The field is only locally clamped at usage sites in nitrogen_cycle.rs (lines 537 and 982). A corrupted save or deserialization with value > 1.0 would pass through enforce_invariants unchecked and could amplify denitrification rate at the calculation site. This is a genuine consistency gap and a real invariant enforcement bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-e08fb6f7","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: cumulative_n2_export_mg_n is a monotonically increasing counter (only += at nitrogen_cycle.rs:570), included in the nitrogen budget array (budget.rs:343-346), but has no check_non_negative validation in validate_invariants_inner. A corrupted save with a negative value would silently unbalance the nitrogen budget. Other cumulative counters and budget-relevant fields are validated; this omission is inconsistent and represents a real defensive gap."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-8f4f8117","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: The process params validation block in invariants.rs validates all other kinetic parameters (aob_vmax, nob_vmax, decomposer_vmax, etc.) but none of the five denitrification params. The call-site uses .max(0.01) and safe_rate() as ad-hoc clamping (nitrogen_cycle.rs:531-538), but this silently masks invalid configs rather than rejecting them at validation time. All other kinetic params are validated upfront in invariants — the denitrification params should follow the same pattern for consistency and early error detection."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-e421d6bc","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: process.rs lines 25-27 still read 'Reserved for E4b (denitrification implementation). When wiring, add alk_produced = n_denitrified_mg * DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N symmetrically to the nitrification deduction path.' However, this constant is actively used at nitrogen_cycle.rs:572 (alk_produced = actual_mg_n * DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N). The stale 'Reserved for' / 'When wiring' language is misleading — it implies future work that is already done. This is a straightforward doc fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-c794c8e0","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: git diff from the root repo only shows changes to the .claude/worktrees/tanksim-6e5.4.7 subpath. The actual implementation changes (nitrogen_cycle.rs, process.rs, engine.rs, water_change.rs, budget.rs, budget_helpers.rs) exist only inside the worktree directory. If the deliverable is measured from the root repo's perspective, none of the tank_core changes would be included in a merge or release. The worktree changes need to be integrated back into the main repo tree to actually ship."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-1a0c886f","decision":"reject","rationale":"Factually incorrect. The main repo already fully implements chloride-aware nitrite hazard in shrimp.rs. The code at shrimp.rs:52-70 contains compute_effective_nitrite_hazard() which applies the formula: effective = [NO2] / (1 + chloride_protection_factor × [Cl] / [NO2]). The step_hourly_shrimp_stress function (line 122-128) calls compute_nitrite_stress_diagnostics with chloride_mg_l and state.shrimp_params.chloride_protection_factor. The species-level chloride_protection_factor exists in biology.rs:315-316 with defaults, and is populated from species presets (e.g., neocaridina_davidi.toml:29 sets it to 0.5). Dedicated tests exist in shrimp_chloride_protection.rs. The amendment's claim that 'shrimp.rs:18-43 still computes hourly_nitrite_stress_accum solely from nitrite_mg_l with no chloride modifier' is wrong — the cited line range does not contain that logic; the actual stress computation at lines 73-128 is fully chloride-aware."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"352935ca-448f-45f0-aab8-d26994463809"}
